+## 8. Executable conventions for the reviewed draft
+
+The implementation is `tools/timing/sweep_analysis.py`; tests are `tools/timing/test_sweep_analysis.py`. Both perform offline analysis only. No implicit newest capture/session selection is allowed for a real trial. Supply an explicit UTC marker, declared session ID(s), and a 100- or 200-press block. The native **physical press ledger**, not surviving JSONL grades, selects the first consecutive block. A missing/ambiguous press record or invalid/conflicting JSONL identity blocks the primary fit. Identical duplicated records/forwarded lines are deduplicated, never counted twice. Epochs/attempts remain integers without a float round trip. Native process partitions follow observed physical-epoch/release-counter resets; rotation files are merged chronologically, not treated as separate processes. Never guess through an identity collision.
+
+Primary release identity requires `Release onsetff`. `Release delivery identity` is a labelled legacy fallback **only** for descriptive widths. A release must match exactly one record by epoch, press-to-close interval, and ±150 ms release timestamp. Attempt/seq/scheduled fields must agree. `Release devoffset`, not the last refinement line, supplies D; all refinements remain auditable in the per-shot output. Distinct arm-token draws are counted once per token; identical forwarded draws are not extra treatments. The last FF covariate timestamp must be **at or before** the record release, not later. A `scheduled=0` release carrying nonzero D or F is inconsistent and quarantined. For retrospective visible endpoints only, `Release landing` matches unique `(process,native seq)` within **0–5,000 ms after release**, even if the banner already closed the JSONL record. Those endpoints are never a pre-fire predictor.
+
+Local H-on-Z fidelity uses **all joined scheduled releases with H**, including missing-banner releases, rather than conditioning on a grade. D-versus-draw agreement is over all scheduled releases; missing D/Z is not agreement. At least 90% of joined scheduled releases must have finite H. A released record with a nonfinite/impossible press-release-close order, negative hold, or more than 1 ms disagreement between hold and wall-clock release minus press is a reported clock failure and blocks the gate, not a silently trimmed shot. Z_final is the release token's draw for this first stage; Z_first remains the policy/attrition/bin assignment. Additional conservative parsing gates require release identity and known scheduled/in-tick status for ≥90% of eligible graded shots; both FF arms must occur in the grade fit. Unknown schedule cannot disappear from the denominator. Invalid draws outside [-25,25] block inference. Report H-on-D too. HC3 intervals use a t critical value with residual degrees of freedom; the 2,000-resample sensitivity samples contiguous blocks of 20 chronological shots (a last partial block is retained, and blocks do not cross session boundaries). These block intervals are not independent-session validation.
+
+The MLE fixes D's coefficient at one; numerical optimisation uses multiple broad/narrow starts and positive W/sigma, stable log-probabilities, and linear positive W(w) over observed widths for the width alternative. Profile intervals invert a 1-df LR threshold 3.841459; a numerical endpoint is reported **open**, not a finite confidence bound. An irregular/boundary primary fit additionally runs 2,000 parametric refits for percentile intervals; this does not repair open profiles or authorise a ceiling claim. Lack-of-fit uses Z_first bins, complete per-replicate refits, and `(1 + exceedances)/(1 + successful simulations)`; fewer than 95% converged simulations gives no p-value. Failed bootstrap/optimisation results are explicit missing results. Random seed **20260922** is frozen. The real CLI does not offer a switch to silently reduce the registered 2,000/10,000 resampling counts.
+
+FF exact permutation uses all arm allocations conditional on the observed arm counts (hypergeometric sufficient statistic for binary policy success); its two-sided statistic is absolute arm-1 minus arm-0 risk difference. G-computation standardises over the same first-assigned-Z covariates for both arms; bootstrap resamples physical epochs, not log lines. Constant nuisance columns are removed, but nonconstant rank deficiency/separation is reported, not silently regularised. Adjusted comparisons with missing Z are explicitly complete-covariate sensitivity analyses; raw policy-success remains primary. Onset/order sensitivity compares to the **same complete-onset cohort** baseline. Explicit-open-only fits supplement, never replace, the stated primary cohort.
+
+Width audit selection is made without grades: compute Z_first quartiles among otherwise width-eligible shots, then select the **first five chronological keys in each of eight arm × Z-quartile cells** (exactly 40; shortage means inconclusive, not replacement based on outcomes). Freeze independent frame annotations as JSON with `blinded:true`, `selected_before_labels:true`, and `rows:[{session,epoch,first_confirmed_width_pp,release_width_pp},...]`; duplicate/wrong keys or release annotations differing by >0.1 pp from the logged one-decimal value invalidate the supplied audit. Use absolute differences for the median≤0.2/p95≤0.5 pp stability thresholds. A claimed blinded annotation is a manual prerequisite, not something a Boolean can prove. The script returns width results as exploratory when the pre-decision gate fails; it reports a full-positive-width sensitivity, quartile first stages, profiles, verdict derivatives, and optimal aim as `(c(w)-delta*A)/(1+gamma*(w-w0))`, not merely c(w). Missing/still-uncertain quartile delivery blocks a physical grade-slope interpretation.
+
+Real-run protocol JSON requires `same_spot:true`, `online_open_standstills:true`, `offset_spec:"uniform:-25:25"`, `ff_spec:"0.2:10:1,0.45:40:0"`, and real `build_sha256`/`settings_sha256`. These are acquisition attestations, not inferred ownership or binary verification. The script checks hook/arm-setting logs and a nonempty, time-overlapping capture `meta.json`/`packets.csv`. It does **not** promote a first-packet proxy to verified delivery, inspect pcap link-layer identity, or implement the later multi-session network/policy-validation extension. Those remain independent gates in sections 3–6. A missing capture fails the planned acquisition protocol; a good capture does not replace the independent local first stage. Dry runs always suppress the randomised primary fit and never fabricate assignments.
+
+The script creates a fresh output directory with `shots.csv` (exact keyed joins and line provenance), `summary.json` (input hashes, fits, gates, distributions, predictions), and `RUN.txt`; it refuses to overwrite prior output and aborts if input hashes change while analysing. A completed legacy dry run exits 0 with `PRIMARY_SUPPRESSED`; a real trial with failed protocol/fidelity exits 2. A statistically analysed run is not automatically approved for shipping or a ceiling claim. Keep source, build, and runtime untouched during this pre-data review.
